# UMML FEATURE 3: Cross-Architecture Spatial Mapping (x86-64)
# Input: x86 Assembly -> Output: UMML Spatial Dataflow

make a memory named reg_rax with size 64
make a memory named reg_rbx with size 64
make a memory named reg_rcx with size 64

# Mapped Instruction: ADD rax, rbx
make a neuron named alu_1 with threshold 1 and leak 0
merge the spike from reg_rbx and reg_rax into the input of alu_1
flow the spike from alu_1 into the write of reg_rax

# Mapped Instruction: SUB rcx, rax
make a neuron named alu_2 with threshold 1 and leak 0
merge the spike from reg_rax and reg_rcx into the input of alu_2
flow the spike from alu_2 into the write of reg_rcx

start the system
